```
Wait `chart.notes` entries have `.t`, `.lane`, `.type`, `.dur`. yes.
```
const delay=Math.max(0,(n.t - now())*1000);
setTimeout(()=>{ if(window.__cryout.state!=='playing') return;
 document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown',{code:codes[n.lane]}));
 const hold=n.type==='hold'?(n.dur||0):0.03;
 setTimeout(()=>document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup',{code:codes[n.lane]})), hold*1000+40);
},delay);
```
But scheduling from t=0 with now() = -0.12 → delay=30.5s. Fine.

Note: setTimeout timers in background tab can throttle, but page is active. We'll periodically bring to front? Headless page is "visible" by default. Should be fine. Playwright's page is not backgrounded.

